==Battleground==
*1 [[Zory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*2 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**1 [[Zory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Similar to [[First Round (Expert)]], just that the [[Doge]] variants are replaced with [[Gory]] variants, and there is now an added [[General GreGory]] and [[Metal Doge]]s, with [[Super Metal Hippoe]] serving as the boss instead of [[Kory]]. Due to the nature of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critical hitters]] are required in order to defeat the Super Metal Hippoe (and you'll need critical hitters anyways if you even want a chance to beat [[Last Round: Dusk (Merciless)]]. The Gories can be held off by strong [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]] like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] and/or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], and the Metal Doges can be dealt with by the critical hitters you bring for the Super Metal Hippoe.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
Since you will face up to four continuation stages, selected from a pool of eight different ones, you will need to select units that can help get you through all of them. The following are the non-Uber units that are the most helpful to do that:
*[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - The best overall meat shields are also the most helpful to have here.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] (Extra Money Talent) - Very high stats for the cost, being able to deal hefty amounts of DPS for as low as 675c, and with talents, can make double the cash on kill.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] (Wave Talent) - There are enough Dark units in the continuation stages to justify running Pizza Cat. In particular, he is crucial to beating [[Last Round: Dawn (Merciless)]]
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] (Savage Blow Talent) - Just like Pizza, there are enough zombies in the continuation stages and long-ranged Backliners like Professor A. in [[4th Round: Dawn (Merciless)]]. She is very powerful at being a sniper and anti-zombie.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - A good all-around unit to have, he also allows you to cheese [[2nd Round: Dusk (Deadly)]] with Manic Erasers and Can Can Cats. Additionally, if you have unlocked his Explosion [[Talents]], he becomes an absolute monster at rushing nearly every stage, even being able to rush down Kurosawah in one cycle in Last Round Dawn at '''Level 30'''.
*[[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] - You'll need to have a high level Soba to consistently beat [[Last Round: Dusk (Merciless)]]. If you still have trouble with Last Round: Dusk (Merciless) you should add in [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]].
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - He's a solid meatshield, and very helpful on both 4th Round stages.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] (Target Angel) - There are a smattering of Angel and Floating units throughout, but like Ramen Cat he helps mainly to get through the Angel/Floating heavy 4th Round stages, but not as needed if you have better crowd-controller Ubers or your Ramen and erasers are tanky enough to solo Boraphim.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] (Slow Up Talent) - Unless you have a very long range Uber, you will need to run Cyberpunk for slow / chip damage.

